    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the volume of the sphere inscribed in a cube with an edge length of 6 inches, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the relationship between the cube and the sphere:**\n   - A sphere is inscribed within a cube when the sphere touches all six faces of the cube.\n   - This implies that the diameter of the sphere equals the edge length of the cube.\n\n2. **Determine the diameter of the sphere:**\n   - Given the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches.\n\n3. **Find the radius of the sphere:**\n   - The radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of its diameter.\n   \\[\n   r = \\frac{\\text{diameter}}{2} = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Use the formula for the volume of a sphere:**\n   - The volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n   \\]\n\n5. **Substitute the radius into the formula:**\n   - Substitute \\( r = 3 \\) inches into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the volume:**\n   - Compute the cube of the radius:\n   \\[\n   3^3 = 27\n   \\]\n   - Multiply the result by \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\):\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27 = 36 \\pi\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe volume of the inscribed sphere is \\(\\boxed{36\\ \\pi}\\) cubic inches.",
